# Ship chain

When the user says deploy, push, or commit, run this chain every time:

1. Create a branch. Do not commit directly to main.
2. Commit the change. Leave tokens, .env files, and Chrome profiles out.
3. Push the branch.
4. Open a detailed pull request into main.
5. Merge with `gh pr merge --admin`.

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --title "the pr title" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- What changed and why

## Test plan
- [ ] How to verify

EOF
)"
gh pr merge --admin --merge
```
